  "lineage": "Singing of the Romanichal, the Romani Gypsies of England, who kept a large repertoire of narrative ballads, broadside and local songs, sung unaccompanied at family gatherings, horse fairs and pubs. Singers recorded from the 1950s onward include Phoebe Smith of Woodbridge in Suffolk and members of Gypsy families in Sussex and Kent, and their recordings were issued in Topic's Voice of the People series.",
